# Pinned STIX bundle: 55 MB, reproducible from build/sources.lock.json via build/fetch_stix.py.
# Its SHA-256 is pinned, so excluding it costs no traceability.
build/cache/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scan output is evidence; it must never be committed.
out/
scan-output/
*.scan.json

# Release binaries: build-time output, not source. README.md and PLAN.md both describe this
# directory as "git-ignored, build-time only", but it was never actually added here, so the
# three files under dist/ got committed in earlier phases. That tracked state is what makes
# `go build` embed a flipping `vcs.modified` flag (Go's automatic VCS stamping sees dist/ as
# dirty right after any rebuild overwrites the previously committed binary), which breaks the
# "built reproducibly" claim for the Linux target -- see the review notes for 2026-10-14.
# Adding the entry here stops new drift; the three already-tracked files still need
# `git rm --cached dist/SHA256SUMS dist/irscan-linux-amd64 dist/irscan-windows-amd64.exe`.
dist/

__pycache__
